# Template for /etc/sponsord/secret.env (root:root 0600). `sudo docker compose up`
# reads it when it creates the container, so the sponsord account never needs to.
# It holds SPONSORD_RPC_URL and nothing else: compose.yaml loads it last, so any
# other key here would override sponsord.env.
#
# FORMAT: Compose's env-file parser, not a shell. One KEY=value per line. Compose
# expands `$VAR` in unquoted and double-quoted values, so single-quote a value
# containing `$`. systemd strips single quotes too and rejects `export`, so leave
# that out and the same file works under the Ansible role.
#
# The RPC endpoint the daemon signs and sends pool top-ups through. It may embed a
# provider API key, which is why it lives here and not in sponsord.env.
SPONSORD_RPC_URL=
